    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Nina has n music sessions in a week. She attends the sessions n days a week x% of\nthe time, n −1 days y% of the time, one day z% of the time, and no days p% of the\ntime. Let, X be a discrete random variable representing the number of sessions she\nattends in a week. Suppose one week is randomly selected, what is the probability that\nthe random variable X takes the value at most n −1?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "1-x/100"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "The only value exceeding n−1 is n, which has probability x/100."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "For x=0,1,2,… let P(X=x)=k(m/n)^x, where 0≤m/n<1. Find k so this is a probability mass function."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "1-m/n"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "The infinite geometric series sums to 1/(1−m/n); normalization requires k=1−m/n, provided 0≤m/n<1."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "prompt": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "For x=0,1,2,… let P(X=x)=k(m/n)^x, where 0≤m/n<1 and k makes the total probability one. Find P(X=2)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "Give an expression in the stated parameters."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "short_answer",
      "acceptable_answers": [
        "(1-m/n)*(m/n)^2",
        "(1-m/n)(m/n)^2",
        "(1-m/n)*(m/n)**2"
      ],
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "With k=1−m/n from normalization, substitute X=2 into the mass function."
        }
      ]
